# Board 4.4. Mail is docked beside Safari. Quitting Mail and opening it again puts it back where it was;
# closing a window does not keep its place.
quiet
open Safari
open Mail
open Notes
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
expect left-of 101 102

# ⌘Q. The neighbours close over the place at once, as for a closed window.
quit-app Mail
expect visible 101
expect count docked 1
wait 20

# Mail again: another process, another window number, the same title.
open Mail
title 104 Mail 102
expect docked 104
expect left-of 101 104

# An update restarts the browser: the process is simply gone, and comes back under another title.
kill-app Safari
wait 5
open Safari
expect docked 105
expect left-of 105 104

# What was done while an app was away stays done, and can be undone with the app in its place.
dock 103 beside 104 bottom
quit-app Safari
resize 103 top 80
open Safari
expect docked 106
expect left-of 106 104
undo
expect docked 106
float 103

# ⌘W is not ⌘Q: Mail lives on, so the place goes, and the next window is a new window.
open Mail
close 104
open Mail
title 108 Mail 102
expect floating 108
wait 10
expect count docked 1

# An app that stays away gets no place for ever.
quit-app Safari
wait 200
open Safari
expect floating 109
